    "html": "<p>A potential difference <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> is maintained between two parallel horizontal plates separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span>. A particle with a constant charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q\"></span> located between the plates experiences an electrostatic force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>. If the potential difference is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4V\"></span> and the separation between the plates is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2d\"></span>, what is the new force acting on the particle?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.5F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8F\"></span></p></li></ol>"
